.TH RUSTY-WAVE 1 "@DATE@" "Rusty Wave @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rusty-wave \- play video and music
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rusty-wave
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR|\fBfile://\fR\fIURI\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rusty-wave
is Rusty Wave: a standalone player for video and music with a library, a queue and a visualizer. It decodes H.264, AV1 and
VP9 video and AAC, MP3, FLAC, Opus, Vorbis and PCM audio in MP4, Matroska, WebM, Ogg, WAV and raw audio files with its own decoders,
so no codec packages are needed.
.PP
Files given on the command line become the queue and the first one plays. Subtitle files (\fI.srt\fR, \fI.vtt\fR) join the video that
is playing and playlist files (\fI.m3u\fR, \fI.m3u8\fR, \fI.pls\fR) are imported. A folder is added to the music library and scanned.
With no arguments the queue and the position of the last run come back, paused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start in full screen.
.TP
.BI \-\-window " WxH"
Initial window size in logical pixels (default 1280x720; otherwise the size of the last run).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Do not open an audio device. Video plays and the clock runs, silently.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-media\-keys
Do not register with MPRIS (Linux) or the System Media Transport Controls (Windows).
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " DIR"
Keep settings, the library index and the saved queue in \fIDIR\fR.
.SS For scripts and tests
.TP
.BI \-\-exit\-after " SEC"
Quit after \fISEC\fR seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " PNG"
Write the window's picture to \fIPNG\fR, at \fB\-\-screenshot\-after\fR seconds or at exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-report " JSON"
Write a short report (state, position, frames shown, audio clock rate) at exit.
.TP
.B \-\-paused
Open the first file paused.
.TP
.BI \-\-press " SEC:KEY"
Press a key \fISEC\fR seconds into the run. May be repeated.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Space, K
Play or pause.
.TP
.B F, F11, Alt+Enter
Full screen.
.TP
.B B
Switch between the player and the music library.
.TP
.B O
Open files.
.TP
.B Left, Right (Shift: 30 s)
Seek 5 seconds; J and L seek 10 seconds.
.TP
.B Up, Down, M
Volume, mute.
.TP
.B [ ], backslash
Slower, faster, normal speed.
.TP
.B S, A
Next subtitle track, next audio track.
.TP
.B N, P, R, Z, Q
Next, previous, repeat, shuffle, the queue.
.TP
.B 1 to 7, V, /
In the library: albums, artists, tracks, playlists, queue, now playing, the visualizer; V also starts the visualizer; / searches.
.PP
Right-click anything for a menu with every action. See the project README for the complete list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rusty-wave/
Settings, the library index, cover thumbnails, the saved queue and resume positions (on Windows
.I %APPDATA%\\rusty-wave\\data\fR).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RVP_REDUCE_MOTION=1
Calmer animations and no beat pulses in the visualizer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a normal exit, 1 if the window could not be opened, 2 for a bad command line.
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/iDoMeteor/rusty-video-player/issues
